The new eating-while-attacked timeout is great...BUT...(you knew this was
coming). I was just gobbling down a hobbit, when a kobold came up to see
how I was doing. I promptly stopped eating. So far, so good. I then went
to hit the kobold, and got the dreaded "You collapse under your load.
The kobold hits --more--"... When I was interrupted, I picked up the
hobbit corpse ( or rather, the program did it for me - I couldn't do it
on my own), and I was overloaded. Shouldn't the hobbit remains stay on
the dungeon floor until I'm done eating? Do we want it to work this way?
(I do). What does the development team think?

